  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Payloads">Files</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Downloading">Downloading</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Verifying">Verifying what is already here…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PayloadsReady">Downloaded and verified.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManifestLocal">The published download list could not be read, so the copy that ships with this app is in use.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManifestFailed">Could not read the download list. Check the connection and try again.</sys:String>

  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Language">Language</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UpdateWorking">Downloading the update…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Dismiss">Not now</sys:String>

  <sys:String x:Key="Str.LogSaved">The full log was written next to this app.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Working">Working…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GamesUnreadable">The list of games could not be read. It was kept as {0} beside it, and a new list started.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CloseWhileBusy">Still writing to a game folder. It takes a few seconds; close the window once it is done.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.FreeTitle">This is free. If you paid for it, you are being scammed.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.FreeBody">Nobody sells any of this — not the installer, not the add-on, not the runtime, not the weights. If you were charged for it, or for a "key" or a "pro version", ask for your money back: what they sold you is on this page for nothing.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.OpenSourceBody">It is open source and it is staying that way: read it, change it, build your own, hand it to your friends. The one thing we ask is that nobody turns it into a paid version.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportSection">Support</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportNote">optional, and it buys nothing</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportKofiTitle">Ko-fi</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportKofiBody">A one-off coffee.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportVakinhaTitle">Vakinha</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportVakinhaBody">The project's Brazilian fundraiser.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportRail">Support AMD-NR</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportTitle">Keep AMD-NR alive</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportBody">This project only stays alive with support from the people who use it. It is two people, two graphics cards and afternoons of work: no company, no sponsor. Everything here is free and stays free. Support unlocks nothing; it keeps the work going.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportBrazil">In Brazil? The Vakinha takes Pix, card or boleto.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditRuntimeTitle">DLSS-NR-on-AMD — by danielblnc</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditRuntimeBody">The network itself, and the reason any of this exists: it is what got DLSS 5's neural rendering running on Radeon at all. The runtime and the weights this app downloads are his work, not ours. Thank you, danielblnc.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditAddonTitle">dlss5-neural-amd — the add-on</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditAddonBody">What plugs that network into a game through ReShade: the add-on this installs, and the releases this offers you a choice of. MIT licensed, and a separate repository from this installer.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditDiscordTitle">Discord — where everyone is</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditDiscordBody">New builds, what works in which game, and where to ask when something breaks.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditsSection">Credits</sys:String>

  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Scan">Scan games</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Scanning">Reading Steam, Epic, GOG, EA, Ubisoft, Battle.net and Xbox…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Search">Search games…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Settings">Settings</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.WillDownload">The files are downloaded and verified when you install.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NoRoute">Nothing this game renders with has a route: the add-on works on D3D11, D3D12, Vulkan and OpenGL, and on D3D8, D3D9 and D3D11 for 32-bit games. A 32-bit OpenGL game, a 64-bit D3D9 one and a software renderer have none.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchRenderer">This game can run on {1}. Set it to {0} in its own graphics settings — that is the route picked here, and on another API the add-on sees a different game.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchRendererUnreal">This is an Unreal game: add -{0} to its launch options.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CheckWiki">Look this game up on PCGamingWiki</sys:String>
  <!-- Feedback and layout -->
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.EmptyTitle">No games yet</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NoMatchTitle">No matches</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NoMatch">No game in the list matches "{0}".</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ScanningShort">Scanning…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ScanDone">Scan finished: {0} games found, {1} new.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstalledBadge">Installed</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Close">Close</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CloseHint">Close (Esc)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeSection">The game's executable</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeChoose">Choose…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeUseDetected">Use the detected one</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNone">No executable found in this folder.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNote">The route is read from this file. If the bitness looks wrong (a launcher in the root, the game in Bin64), point it at the right .exe.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNoteChosen">You chose this file, so detection leaves it alone, even after a rescan.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNotHere">That file is not inside this game's folder.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeUnreadable">That file is not a Windows executable this can read.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteMismatch">This route is for {0} games and the executable above is {1}. Nothing stops you — the detection may have read the wrong file — but if it read the right one, this will not load.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionSection">Add-on version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxySection">ReShade loads as</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyNote">Automatic uses dxgi.dll, which serves every Direct3D. Change it only if the game refuses to load it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxySectionOpti">OptiScaler loads as</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyNoteOpti">Automatic uses the first name the OptiScaler wiki gives for this game, or else the one already in use here, or else dxgi.dll. Pick winmm.dll to keep another program's dxgi.dll.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyAuto">Automatic</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyAutoWiki">Automatic (wiki: {0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PrefetchAll">Download all now</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCache">Clear the cache</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheBody">Deletes the downloaded files, the covers and the version list. Nothing installed in a game is touched; the next install downloads what it needs again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheYes">Clear it</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheYesBody">Everything in it is downloaded again the next time you install.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheNoBody">Leave the cache as it is.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CacheCleared">Cache emptied — {0} freed.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PayloadsAlreadyThere">Everything was already there, and every byte just checked out.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionShipped">bundled</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteShipped">The version this installer was published with.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteRelease">From the v{0} release on GitHub, checked against its hashes.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionSectionOpti">OptiScaler version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteOpti">OptiScaler {0}, from its GitHub release, every file checked against its hash.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteOptiLmxxf">Includes the lmxxf weights (about 590 MB, RDNA4 only).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteOptiMochizuki">Can also bring mochizuki: see NR runtime.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiSection">NR runtime</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DanielVersion">danielblnc version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RuntimeRecommended">Recommended</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RuntimeUnstable">Unstable</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DanielVersionTip">Which version of danielblnc's runtime goes into this game. On RX 9000 cards 0.4.3 is the recommended one: the newer ones have frozen games there. Other cards get the newest.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RuntimeRdna4Addon">RX 9000: mochizuki (mochizuki0323's Vulkan port, about 141 MB) goes in too and runs the network. danielblnc's runtime stays beside it: pick it under NR runtime in the add-on's panel. The first start in each game compiles the network for up to a minute.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RuntimeRdna4Opti">RX 9000: a new install runs lmxxf, and mochizuki (about 141 MB) goes in beside danielblnc's runtime. Pick another under NR runtime in OptiScaler's Neural tab and restart the game.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickRouteTitle">Pick a route to install with</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickRouteBody">This app could not tell which graphics API {0} renders with, so it does not pick a route for you. OptiScaler is the one for a D3D12 game that offers DLSS, FSR or XeSS in its settings; ReShade, on D3D11 or D3D12, is the one for any other. Install waits until you pick.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickRouteBodyAll">This app could not tell which graphics API {0} renders with, so it does not pick a route for you. OptiScaler runs on 64-bit D3D9, D3D11, D3D12, Vulkan and OpenGL games, inside the game's DLSS, FSR or XeSS when it has one; ReShade also covers 32-bit games, emulators and D3D10. Install waits until you pick.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickRouteDetail">The graphics API is unknown, so the route is yours to pick below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterTitle">danielblnc's runtime</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterChoose">Which runtime build goes into this game. The highlighted card is the one used.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterDownloadTitle">Public Release ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterDownloadBody">Downloaded and verified by this app.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterBuildTitle">Local Supporter Build ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPick">Choose my version.dll or setup…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPickOther">Choose another file…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPitch">Newer than the Public Release, from your own version.dll or danielblnc's setup.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPitch.0.5.0">0.5.0 adds kernels for RDNA3 cards.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPitch.0.6.0">0.6.0 adds RX 6000 (RDNA2) cards, which need AMD's HIP SDK 7.2 runtime, and fixes flicker in dark areas and on small lights.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterNotDistributed">Never downloaded or shared by this app. Your file is checked by SHA-256 and kept, so other games do not ask again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUse">Use my supporter files…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUseDownload">Public Release</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPickTitle">Your version.dll or dlssnr_on_amd_setup.exe</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterFiles">version.dll, dlssnr_on_amd_setup.exe</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterAnyFile">Any DLL or setup</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUsingDownload">In use: the runtime this app downloads.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUsingFile">Using {0} from your file.</sys:String>
